{{Short description|Football tournament knockout stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
The knockout stage of [[1978 FIFA World Cup]] was a [[single-elimination tournament]] involving the four teams that qualified from [[1978 FIFA World Cup#Second round|the second group stage of the tournament]]. There were two matches: a match for third place contested by the group runners-up, and the final to decide the champions, contested by the group winners.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/78full.html |title=World Cup 1978 finals |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref> The knockout stage began with the match for third place on 24 June and ended with the [[1978 FIFA World Cup final|final]] on 25 June 1978, both at the [[Estadio Monumental Antonio Vespucio Liberti|Estadio Monumental]] in [[Buenos Aires]]. [[Argentina national football team|Argentina]] won the tournament with a 3–1 victory over the [[Netherlands national football team|Netherlands]].<ref>{{Cite web|url = http://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/legacy/jonathanstevenson/2010/05/the_story_of_the_1978_world_cu.html|title=The story of the 1978 World Cup |date=18 May 2010|work=BBC Sport|accessdate=30 April 2014}}</ref>

==Qualified teams==
The top two placed teams from each of the two groups of the second round qualified for the knockout stage.

